# BlockML Libraries & Versioning

## Library structure

- Abstract base type: `org.blockml.BlockLibrary` (`packages/core/blocks/org/blockml/BlockLibrary.bml`)
- Every real library: `<name>Library</name>`, filename **`Library.bml`**
- FQN = `{package}.Library` from the file's package path
- `baseType="blockml:BlockLibrary"` on concrete Library blocks
- **Membership is defined only by `Library.bml` `_blocks`** — not by directories or package overlap

## Nested libraries

Multiple `Library.bml` files may exist at different package levels (e.g. `org.blockml.Library` + `org.blockml.compiler.Library`).

```text
Typical:  inner _dependencies → outer Library
Forbidden: outer _blocks → Block exported by inner Library
Error:    BML_LIBRARY_NESTING_VIOLATION
```

A `.bml` file physically under `org/blockml/compiler/` belongs to `org.blockml.compiler.Library` only if listed in **that** library's `_blocks` — not in `org.blockml.Library` just because of directory.

## Effective block version

```text
effectiveBlockVersion =
  own <version>       if present
  else library.version if exported via Library _blocks
  else error → BML_MISSING_VERSION
```

- **Framework blocks** (`org.blockml.*`, `com.machineblocks.*`): version only on `Library.bml`
- **Block in library** with own `<version>`: must be `>= library.version`
- **Standalone block**: `<version>` mandatory

## Instance references (`bml:version`)

- **Optional** on external references — omitted = resolve from TypeRegistry context
- **Present** = exact-version assert → `BML_UNKNOWN_VERSION` if no match
- **Forbidden** inside Library `_dependencies` / `_blocks` → `BML_VERSION_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_LIBRARY`

## Library file pattern

```xml
<name>Library</name>
<baseType>blockml:BlockLibrary</baseType>
<version>3.0.0</version>
<_dependencies>
  <composition><blockml:Library /></composition>  <!-- inner depends on outer -->
</_dependencies>
<_blocks>
  <composition><compiler:Parser /></composition>   <!-- own blocks only -->
</_blocks>
```
